# An effect that ends the turn during the cleanup step begins a new cleanup step (CR 724.1d). Bot1 refills its hand with
# Wheel of Fortune and Ancestral Recall and ends turn 3 with nine cards: it discards two at cleanup, which triggers
# Marauding Mako, so players get priority in the cleanup step (CR 514.3a). Bot1 activates Sundial of the Infinite there
# (it is still Bot1's turn): the Mako's ability is exiled from the stack (724.1b) and never puts its counters on. A new
# cleanup step begins, in which Bot1, at seven cards, discards nothing and nothing triggers, so no one gets priority and
# turn 4 is Bot2's.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Sundial of the Infinite
Marauding Mako
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Wheel of Fortune
Ancestral Recall
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x30

